From u8c45483022d450d5 at groups.google.com  Thu Aug 25 09:18:40 2011
From: u8c45483022d450d5 at groups.google.com (Matthieu)
Date: Thu, 25 Aug 2011 09:18:40 +0000
Subject: Groupwise weighted mean?
Message-ID: <FhvnHex9uNs.qQMfoQViIXcJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/FhvnHex9uNs/m/qQMfoQViIXcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi

I have a hopefully simple question :-) I want to do groupwise weighted
means. The problem is that I guess ddply() takes the weight variable
among the whole data.frame, not among groups... how can I specify
this?

DF<-data.frame(a=rnorm(5), b=rnorm(5),size=rnorm(5, mean=200, sd=40),
group=sample(letters[1:2], 5, replace=TRUE))

means<-ddply(DF, .(group), numcolwise(mean), na.rm = T)
w.means<-ddply(DF, .(group), numcolwise(weighted.mean), na.rm = T, w=.
(size))

How do I tell ddpla .(size) has to be taken among grops?

Thanks!

Matthieu

From udc06d729e023580a at groups.google.com  Thu Aug 25 11:56:56 2011
From: udc06d729e023580a at groups.google.com (Hadley Wickham)
Date: Thu, 25 Aug 2011 11:56:56 +0000
Subject: Re: Groupwise weighted mean?
Message-ID: <FhvnHex9uNs.xr4zgua9C6IJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <FhvnHex9uNs.qQMfoQViIXcJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
References: <FhvnHex9uNs.qQMfoQViIXcJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/FhvnHex9uNs/m/xr4zgua9C6IJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You need to be a little more verbose so you can be more explicit about
where size comes from:

w.means<-ddply(DF, .(group), function(df) {
   numcolwise(weighted.mean)(df, na.rm = T, w=df$size)
})

Hadley

